COMMAND: read key source files with sed/rg
OUTPUT SUMMARY:
app/main.py creates FastAPI app, DB engine/session factory, optional CacheService, CoreRequestPipeline factory, AsyncTaskWorker and NotificationWorker background tasks when async_worker_enabled and schema exists.
app/config.py defines Settings with env_prefix ANH_DUONG_, DB path, OpenClaw URLs/tokens, async worker knobs, and cache flags.
app/api/health.py exposes /health and /ready.
app/api/prepared_requests.py exposes POST /api/internal/requests/prepare behind internal bearer.
app/api/async_tasks.py exposes POST/GET/list/retry/cancel under /api/async-tasks behind internal bearer.
app/orchestration/pipeline.py sequences persona -> FastRouter -> CapabilityRouter -> context builder -> optional workflow envelope -> audit.
app/orchestration/workflow.py maps workflow requests to durable AsyncTaskCreate shape and policy decision.
app/routing/fast_router.py is deterministic phrase router: direct, memory, core_read, workflow.
app/capabilities/router.py maps route+text into typed capability kinds and fail-closed unknown workflow when inconsistent.
app/context_builder/_builder_impl.py builds sections, retrieves memory, estimates/truncates context by token budget, redacts source refs.
app/memory/repository.py implements SQLite memory persistence with FTS5 external-content search and redaction.
app/memory/retrieval.py ranks FTS candidates using lexical/importance/confidence/recency hybrid score.
app/cache/service.py coordinates L1 and L2; cache disabled short-circuits; L2 SQLite is fail-open.
app/openclaw/executor.py sends /v1/responses payload model openclaw/default with idempotency key and parses output_text into OpenClawExecutionResult.
app/openclaw/notifier.py sends final Telegram message through /tools/invoke.
app/policy/engine.py defines risk catalog and approval/deny semantics; app/policy/path_scope.py restricts paths to allowed WSL roots.
app/audit/redaction.py redacts secret-like keys, bearer tokens, query secrets, and provider token shapes; app/audit/writer.py appends JSONL with fsync.

